				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&5Draconic Evolution"
			x: 0.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The &eDraconic Sword&r and &eDraconic Pickaxe&r are the tier-one lineup - draconium-forged, and already a serious step past netherite."
				""
				"&c&lRemember what it cost to get here.&r In this pack the &7Draconium Core&r at the root of this tree is pinned with a &7Silver Dungeon Key&r - so every item in this chapter is downstream of killing the Valkyrie Queen, who will not even fight you until you have collected her Valkyries' Victory Medals."
				""
				"&e&lThe tier ladder above this:&r"
				"&7Draconic &8→&7 &fWyvern&7 &8→&7 &fDraconic (awakened)&7 &8→&7 &fChaotic&r"
				""
				"Each step is a &7Fusion Crafting&r operation - a core surrounded by injectors, fed enormous amounts of FE. Set that multiblock up now; everything from here uses it."
				""
				"&e&lTier-one gear already outclasses netherite&r on raw stats, but the real jump comes at Wyvern when upgrade modules unlock. Do not over-invest in enchanting this tier - you will replace it."
				""
				"&8Draconium comes from the Draconium ore that does not spawn in a void world - which is what SkyForge's bridge recipes and Mystical Agriculture seeds are for. Set up a farm before committing to this chapter."
			]
			icon: "draconicevolution:draconic_sword"
			id: "5739033CBC45ADCC"
			rewards: [{
				id: "3B384F5D4741DDFB"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Tier I &8· Draconic"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "3EF0C4DCD09F7267"
					item: "draconicevolution:draconic_sword"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "64A74CB1DA0C7F42"
					item: "draconicevolution:draconic_pickaxe"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&5Draconic Tools"
			x: -2.0d
			y: -0.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"An &eEnergy Core&r paired with an &eEnergy Pylon&r ring is Draconic Evolution's answer to RF storage - millions of FE, buffered in one structure."
				""
				"&e&lIt is a tiered multiblock, and the tiers are enormous.&r Tier 1 is a single core block. Tier 8 is a vast sphere of Draconium and Wyvern blocks holding a genuinely absurd amount of energy - far more than an Induction Matrix at comparable effort."
				""
				"&e&lHow to build one:&r place the core, then use the &7Energy Core Stabilizer&r blocks at the tier's required offsets. Right-click the core with a &7Crafting Injector&r-style tool to open the build guide - it renders a ghost preview of exactly where every block goes. Do not try to place a tier 4+ core from memory."
				""
				"&e&lEnergy Pylons are the input and output.&r The core itself has no connections. Place pylons facing the core, then toggle each one to input or output mode by right-clicking. A core with no output pylon stores power forever and gives you none of it back - which is the usual reason a new one looks broken."
				""
				"&7Wireless Energy Crystals can move power in and out without cables, which is how most people feed one.&r"
				""
				"&8Build tier 3 or 4 first. It is enough to buffer a fission reactor and costs a fraction of the higher tiers."
			]
			icon: "draconicevolution:energy_core"
			id: "2F22A3FE8C075F7E"
			rewards: [{
				id: "65442B26A6E4CFAC"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 40
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Store power at scale"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "339338EA58C6F451"
					item: "draconicevolution:energy_core"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "69B7253AE046D1F0"
					item: "draconicevolution:energy_pylon"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&5Energy Core"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&eWyvern&r tier gear picks up upgrade modules - flight, auto-feed, shield capacity - turning your tools and armour into a build-your-own loadout."
				""
				"&e&lUpgrades are applied at a Fusion Crafting setup&r and each has multiple levels. You are not choosing a fixed item - you are spending resources to specialise it:"
				"&7- &fShield Capacity / Recovery&7 - a rechargeable damage buffer over your health"
				"&7- &fFlight&7 - creative-style flight once you reach the right tier"
				"&7- &fDig Speed / AOE&7 - the pickaxe mines 3x3, 5x5, and further"
				"&7- &fAuto-Feed&7 - eats from your inventory so you never starve mid-build"
				""
				"&e&lThe AOE upgrade is the one that changes your life.&r A Wyvern pickaxe on 5x5 clears platforms and terrain faster than any Builder card, and it works in every dimension without setup."
				""
				"&c&lEverything here runs on stored FE.&r Flat gear is ordinary gear - the shield stops, the flight stops, and you fall. Keep a charged Energy Cube or a wireless crystal on you."
				""
				"&7Configure active upgrades with the module GUI keybind rather than re-crafting. Most upgrades can be toggled on the fly.&r"
			]
			icon: "draconicevolution:wyvern_sword"
			id: "28E31AAB6A65F788"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7B693D117F397DCB"
				type: "xp_levels"
				xp_levels: 4
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Tier II &8· Wyvern"
