			x: -4.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"The &eDraconic Reactor&r produces more power than anything else in the pack - and detonates spectacularly if mishandled."
				""
				"&e&lThe structure:&r a Reactor Core with four &7Stabilizers&r arranged symmetrically around it, plus injectors for fuel and a way to draw the output."
				""
				"&c&lIt requires active management.&r Temperature, field strength and saturation all interact. Field strength must stay high or containment fails; temperature must stay in band or output collapses. It consumes power to hold containment even while producing."
				""
				"&c&lA failed reactor destroys a very large area.&r Build it away from your base, and build the monitoring before you build the reactor."
				""
				"&7Flux Gates and a Potentiometer let you regulate input and output precisely. Most people wire it through a computer for automatic control - Advanced Peripherals can read and adjust it.&r"
			]
			icon: "draconicevolution:reactor_core"
			id: "27087C30DAC48B35"
			rewards: [{
				id: "51C11704B336E6B9"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Enormous power, real consequences"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "41D2314DAD78E5DB"
					item: "draconicevolution:reactor_core"
					type: "item"
				}
				{
					id: "0EF9E1057F4B252D"
					item: "draconicevolution:reactor_stabilizer"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&5Draconic Reactor"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"A &eFlux Gate&r limits energy flow to an exact rate you set; &eRelay Crystals&r move power wirelessly between linked points."
				""
				"&e&lFlux Gates are how you tame the reactor.&r Two gates - one controlling input to the containment field, one controlling output - are the standard reactor control setup."
				""
				"&7They also stop a huge Energy Core dumping its entire contents into a small machine and melting your grid.&r"
				""
				"&8Relay Crystals are Draconic's answer to Ender Cells and RFTools Power Cells: wireless energy with no cable."
			]
			icon: "draconicevolution:flux_gate"
			id: "41B23D03B3554190"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7BDCA00F566D1AC7"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Precise power control"
			tasks: [{
				id: "1DF5E2102E9EBE6E"
				item: "draconicevolution:flux_gate"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&5Flux Gates & Relays"
			x: -2.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Draconic tools are upgradeable at a &eFusion Crafting&r setup, and the upgrades are what make them extraordinary."
				""
				"&e&lThe one that changes everything is AOE.&r A Wyvern pickaxe at high AOE mines 5x5 or larger per swing; the Draconic and Chaotic tiers go further still."
				""
				"&e&lOther upgrades:&r Dig Speed, Durability, Attack Damage, and on armour - Shield Capacity, Shield Recovery, Flight and Movement Speed."
				""
				"&c&lEverything runs on stored FE.&r Flat gear is ordinary gear, and flight cutting out mid-air is exactly as bad as it sounds. Carry a charged Energy Cube or use a Powah Player Transmitter."
				""
				"&7Configure AOE and other toggles with the tool config key rather than recrafting.&r"
			]
			icon: "draconicevolution:draconic_pickaxe"
			id: "213822B244303C9A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "526313B9CD88DCFC"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Mining at absurd scale"
			tasks: [{
				id: "52673CB2C5F4F860"
				item: "draconicevolution:wyvern_pickaxe"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&5Draconic Tools"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"Draconic armour provides a &eshield&r - a rechargeable buffer that absorbs damage before your health does - and, at the right tier, &eflight&r."
				""
				"&e&lShield Capacity and Shield Recovery are the two upgrades that matter.&r Capacity sets how much damage it soaks; Recovery sets how fast it comes back. A well-upgraded set makes most of this pack's combat trivial."
				""
				"&7Flight here is creative-style, not elytra gliding. It is the most convenient movement in the pack and it costs power constantly.&r"
				""
				"&8Combined with the MekaSuit's modules, you have two competing endgame armour sets. Pick one and invest - splitting resources across both leaves you with neither."
			]
			icon: "draconicevolution:draconium_ingot"
			id: "6C9C3920B9DB9E84"
			rewards: [{
				id: "4DA3A8FA66F864CD"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Flight and a shield that regenerates"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4F54A753B08E2FE9"
				item: "draconicevolution:draconium_ingot"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&5Draconic Armour"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"&eChaos Shards&r come from Chaos Islands in the End - guarded by a Chaos Guardian, one of the hardest fights available."
				""
				"&e&lThis is the top of the Draconic ladder.&r Chaotic-tier tools and armour, and the Draconic Reactor's best fuel, all trace back here."
				""
				"&c&lThe Chaos Guardian is a genuine endgame fight&r - it flies, it summons crystals that must be destroyed to damage it, and it hits extremely hard. Bring Draconic armour, not Wyvern."
				""
				"&7A shard splits into fragments, so one kill supplies several crafts.&r"
			]
			icon: "draconicevolution:chaos_shard"
			id: "23F51DBA84480419"
			rewards: [{
				id: "31F59CB524E2033E"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7The last material"
